config BR2_PACKAGE_V4L2LOOPBACK_OPENIPC
	bool "v4l2loopback-openipc"
	depends on BR2_LINUX_KERNEL
	help
	  Kernel module that creates virtual V4L2 devices: one program
	  writes frames in, any V4L2 reader sees a camera. The seam
	  between a CPU transcoder and v4l2rtspserver when the real USB
	  camera offers no format the network can carry.

	  A fork of buildroot's own package, minus its kernel config
	  fixups: those force CONFIG_MEDIA_SUPPORT and CONFIG_VIDEO_DEV
	  to =y, and on ssc338q that puts the kernel over its 2048KB
	  partition. This tree's board configs carry them as =m.

	  Load with: modprobe v4l2loopback devices=1 video_nr=10
	  card_label=<name> exclusive_caps=1

	  https://github.com/umlaeute/v4l2loopback
